  "mechanismSummary": "Toluenesulfonic acid protonates the ketone of the new ring, and tosylate removes a proton from the CH₂ next to the OH-bearing carbon, giving the enol. The OH is protonated, and the enol pushes water out: the acid version of the E1cB dehydration of the Robinson annulation. Tosylate removes the last proton, giving the conjugated enone, the Wieland–Miescher ketone. Water is removed with a Dean–Stark trap. Acid is used rather than base because base could also run the aldol backwards to the achiral triketone and erode the enantiomeric excess; acid leaves the quaternary stereocentre alone. With (S)-proline in hot acetonitrile and perchloric acid (Eder, Sauer and Wiechert), aldol and dehydration happen in one pot.",
